Route WAV/FLAC saves through soundfile instead of torchaudio.

torchaudio 2.10 routes `torchaudio.save` through torchcodec, whose ffmpeg
libraries collide with the system glib here and segfault the server on the
first save. The client asks for WAV and transcodes with the ffmpeg CLI
afterwards, so only the wav/wav32/flac branch of AudioSaver changes; every
other format still goes through torchaudio. See designs/hosting.md,
"ACE-Step", 2026-08. Against ACE-Step/ACE-Step-1.5 @ 82252c24.

